&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage project scope, schedules, resources, customer expectations, risks, issues, and multiple priorities while delivering concise executive-level status reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build effective relationships with customer leaders, communicate with internal and external stakeholders, and manage escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify and resolve project challenges, motivate advisory teams and contributors, and mediate conflicts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting timely revenue recognition and executing change orders when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of project management and technical delivery methods for software, including Project Management Institute methodologies, agile or Scrum, the software development lifecycle, and project management or agile tools such as GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise customer and Professional Services experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
